00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.780
With its own supercomputer, Walmart streamlined its supply chain,

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:06.700
speeding delivery from plant to store shelf.

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:13.150
The sale's recorded, and then an order is automatically generated that evening at midnight,

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:18.450
and that warehouse fills that order, and it's sitting back on the shelf the next night or the following night.

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:24.750
Walmart became a world leader in logistics and promoted greater efficiency among its suppliers.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:29.060
Some analysts even credit Walmart with increasing U.S. productivity.

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:38.630
Walmart, as an efficiency machine, has just done better than any other U.S. retailer or perhaps any other U.S. company in history.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:45.710
With other mass retail chains like Target and Kmart, Walmart generated a revolution in how goods are produced.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:50.110
A shift from what's called push production to pull production.

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:59.980
The push system involves manufacturers deciding what they're going to produce and then trying to get...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:08.200
retailers to buy it and sell it for them. The pull system involves retailers deciding what is

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:15.050
being sold, collecting information on what is being sold, and then telling manufacturers what

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:21.910
to produce and when to produce it based on what is actually being sold. Walmart's pull is so powerful

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:28.800
that here in Bentonville, manufacturers have set up satellite sales offices in what's now known as

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:29.340
Vanderville.

