And it's headed even higher this year.

00:38:41.270 --> 00:38:50.220
The myth of an enormous and growing China market wound up locking the United States into a trading partnership with China

00:38:50.370 --> 00:38:54.550
that had to benefit China much more than it could benefit us.

00:38:54.670 --> 00:38:55.050
Because?

00:38:55.150 --> 00:38:59.970
And the reason was, China would always be able to sell the United States much more.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:05.140
more goods than Americans could sell to Chinese because Americans had the

00:39:05.140 --> 00:39:09.980
incomes that are needed to buy Chinese products. Chinese consumers overwhelmingly

00:39:09.980 --> 00:39:14.580
don't have the incomes needed to buy American products. So the whole idea was

00:39:14.580 --> 00:39:19.040
was wrong. It was completely wrong. When you look at the growth of the trade

00:39:19.040 --> 00:39:22.720
deficit with China you can say that a very conservative estimate is that we

00:39:22.720 --> 00:39:28.230
have lost more than a million jobs to China since the early 1990s. I think it's

00:39:28.230 --> 00:39:29.830
It's impossible to say that we've lost a million.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:36.170
jobs to China. Trade policy or trade flows one way or another don't have an effect on overall

00:39:36.170 --> 00:39:42.410
employment numbers. They affect the kinds of jobs we have. And so some number of jobs have definitely

00:39:42.410 --> 00:39:48.570
been eliminated because of Chinese competition. Elsewhere in the economy, other jobs have been

00:39:48.570 --> 00:39:53.130
created because of Chinese competition. Because American consumers have saved at Walmart buying

00:39:53.130 --> 00:39:56.810
Chinese goods, they've got more money in their pocket to buy something else, which creates

00:39:56.810 --> 00:39:59.650
business opportunities for those other businesses, which means they hire.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:04.600
workers they would not have hired otherwise. The net effect, most economists think, is a wash.

00:40:05.090 --> 00:40:10.480
Theoretically, the gains from trade offset the losses from trade. But nothing says that there

00:40:10.480 --> 00:40:15.600
are more winners than losers. And nothing says that for the bottom three-fourths of America

00:40:15.600 --> 00:40:20.860
that they are net gainers. In fact, I believe that most people have been losers from trade.

00:40:21.120 --> 00:40:29.980
The impact of China's export boom has

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:32.100
It's been felt all across the U.S.

00:40:35.070 --> 00:40:41.300
Towns like Circleville, Ohio, population 13,000.

