00:41:13.360 --> 00:41:14.720
That came in the 1970s.

00:41:14.870 --> 00:41:17.680
So you had good living standards, good jobs.

00:41:17.840 --> 00:41:21.780
Good jobs, good living standards, and good people in the community.

00:41:22.550 --> 00:41:29.430
The French firm, Thompson, which manufactures TV sets, had the largest plant in town, and it was a top performer.

00:41:30.350 --> 00:41:39.700
The Circleville plant in its heyday, probably around 1999, 2000, was producing about 10 million pieces a year for the production of television sets.

00:41:39.940 --> 00:41:47.230
They made the glass components, about 1,000 workers, highly motivated, highly productive, very efficient plant.

00:41:47.450 --> 00:41:52.110
And at the time, it was one of the most profitable contributors to Thompson's corporate bottom line.

00:41:52.890 --> 00:41:57.390
Steve Ratcliffe was among the 1,000 workers who rode the economic wave with Thompson.

00:41:57.390 --> 00:41:59.960
As a machine operator, he made up...

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:02.640
to $59,000 a year with overtime.

